I wrote the assessment to session_plan/assessment.md (9.5 KB) but did not commit it. session_plan/ is gitignored, so the commit step you gave was a no-op. I first forced the file in with git add -f, then realised that would commit an ignored directory, so I undid my own unpushed commit with a soft reset. HEAD is back at 721150bd and the file is still on disk for the planner.

What the planner most needs:
• Two files are close to failing the module-size gate, which would revert a whole task:
  • src/config.rs is 4851 lines against a recorded 4762. 11 more lines and cargo test fails.
  • src/commands_risk_unhittable.rs is 2036 lines and not on the exceptions list. 14 more lines and it fails.
  • src/prompt_retry.rs is exactly at its recorded limit of 2786.
• The creator's commit `721150bd` changes how planning works. Issues labelled parked no longer count as backlog. Each session should also review one issue with 5+ comments: finish it, or split it and close it. #1012 (19 comments) and #1037 (17) are the biggest candidates.
• The self-driven task should avoid `cli`. It took 6 of the last 10 self-driven changes. Two options outside it:
  • Network-error handling (#1115, in the prompt code).
  • Today's /cost sub-agent wiring (#1108). Its REPL path was only checked by the compiler, and tests/sub_agent_usage_record.rs is probably the stub to extend for a real test.

What I ran:
• yoyo -p with a one-line prompt works.
• New finding: pointing yoyo at a host that can't exist (nonexistent.invalid) takes 1m13s of six retries before giving up. A failed DNS lookup like that won't fix itself, much like the localhost "connection refused" case fixed earlier today. Exit code is 1. The error line is still the raw reqwest::Error { … } dump, which confirms one half of #1115. The other half, REPL /retry advice, didn't appear: on this path no hint was printed at all.
• The 01:12 evolve run on Nov 2 failed. Its log is gone ("log not found") and no step is marked as the failure, so I couldn't find the cause. The other recent runs passed.

Research:
• Claude Code 2.1.316 (2.1.315 isn't in its changelog) has three things yoyo may lack:
  • It now kills its shell commands when it exits on its own, for example after credentials are refused. yoyo only does this for /bg kill and /quit; the bash tool's children on an error exit are untested.
  • It added a separate effort setting for sub-agents. yoyo has a sub-agent model setting but no effort setting.
  • /model with an unrecognised id now warns. yoyo's REPL /model likely already warns, because every agent rebuild runs the guessed-limits check, but I didn't test it.
• Codex 0.166 added codex doctor --network-only and GPT-6.1 Terra. I didn't check whether yoyo's model and price lists include Terra.
